Recommendations on the Transport of Dangerous Goods — UN Model Regulations (@cs-orange: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06
United Nations. Recommendations on the Transport of Dangerous Goods: Model Regulations, twenty-fourth revised edition, September 2025. [Official publication and volumes](https://unece.org/info/transport/Dangerous-Goods/pub/407574).

Read both volumes for a sustained transport study, then revisit the actual classification, goods-list entry, special provisions, packaging/tank, marking, documentation and transport-operation passages applicable to the chosen supplied material. A chemical name alone does not identify every concentration, mixture or transport condition.

The official 2025 edition record was verified on 29 October 2026; it provides free non-editable consultation copies and directs reproduction, mirroring and translation requests to UN rights procedures. No CC licence or inspection of every entry is claimed. Model recommendations and the legislation actually adopted by a route's jurisdictions are distinct. References remain external and should be rechecked for the intended shipment date.

**Return:** [Chemical supply sources — books, methods, complete cases and research](../Sources.lingua#r_76J82CV79QKHQ2CSCT63MFYJYN).
